# Implementation Plan - Auth Flow Refinement

Refine the authentication experience to gracefully handle duplicate signups and allow for the creation of administrative roles.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Graceful Signup Redirection**: When a user attempts to sign up with an existing email, the system will now automatically switch to the Login screen and notify the user. This avoids unnecessary errors and guides them to the correct action.

## Proposed Changes

### Auth Screen Improvements

#### [MODIFY] [AuthScreen.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/src/screens/AuthScreen.tsx)
- Update [handleAuth](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/src/screens/AuthScreen.tsx#85-227) to check for `authError` messages indicative of an existing account (e.g., "User already registered").
- If a duplicate email is detected:
    - Show a success-style toast or a helpful tip: "You already have an account! Switching to login..."
    - Call `setIsSignUp(false)` to update the UI state.
    - Preserve the email in the input field.

### Onboarding Selection Expansion

#### [MODIFY] [OnboardingScreen.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/src/screens/OnboardingScreen.tsx)
- Add `founder` and `admin` roles to the `SelectContent` for the role selection step.

### BDD Verification

#### [NEW] [auth_refinement.feature](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/src/features/auth_refinement.feature)
- Scenario: Attempting signup with an existing email.
- Scenario: Selecting administrative roles during onboarding.

